<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick, Margrave of Brandenburg-Bayreuth</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1711–1763</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick was Margrave of Brandenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayreuth">Bayreuth</a> from 1735 to 1763 and husband of Wilhelmine, sister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-the-great">Frederick the Great</a>. Together they made Bayreuth a centre of art and music, building the Margravial Opera House, now a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>, and new palaces. In 1742 he founded a university at Bayreuth, moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erlangen">Erlangen</a> the next year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-margrave-of-brandenburg-bayreuth.jpg" alt="Frederick, Margrave of Brandenburg-Bayreuth" width="320" height="408" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_438_Friedrich_III_von_Brandenburg-Bayreuth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
